# Platform components — Docker Compose stack

A detailed guide to every **non-application** component in `using-docker/`:
the data stores and message broker the services depend on, and the full
observability stack that watches them. For each one: what it is, why it is
here, real-world use cases, exactly how it is configured in this repo, how to
use it, and what usually goes wrong.

The eight application services (api-gateway, product, cart, order, payment,
inventory, notification, frontend) and the load generator are out of scope —
see the [README](../README.md) for those.

All paths are relative to `using-docker/`.

