## 1. Big picture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph apps[Application services]
    gw[api-gateway] & product & cart & order & payment & inventory & notify[notification]
  end

  subgraph data[Data & messaging]
    pg[(PostgreSQL)]
    mongo[(MongoDB)]
    redis[(Redis)]
    mq{{RabbitMQ}}
  end

  product --> mongo
  cart --> redis
  order & payment & inventory --> pg
  order & payment & inventory & notify <--> mq

  apps -- "OTLP (traces + metrics)" --> col[OTel Collector]
  col -- traces --> jaeger[Jaeger]
  col -- "app + span metrics :8889" --> prom[Prometheus]

  subgraph exporters[Infra exporters]
    cad[cAdvisor] & pge[postgres-exporter] & rde[redis-exporter] & mge[mongodb-exporter]
  end
  exporters --> prom
  mq -- ":15692 plugin" --> prom

  stdout[container stdout/stderr] --> promtail[Promtail] --> loki[Loki]

  prom & jaeger & loki --> grafana[Grafana]
```

Two simple rules explain the whole design:

1. **Applications only know one address for telemetry**: the OpenTelemetry
   Collector (`http://otel-collector:4318`). Where the data goes after that is
   the collector's business. Changing vendor = editing one YAML file.
2. **Infrastructure is observed from the outside**: databases, the broker and
   containers are *scraped* by Prometheus through exporters, and logs are
   *tailed* from Docker by Promtail. Nothing in the databases or the apps has
   to change for that.

