## 2. The three signals: metrics, logs, traces

| | Metrics | Logs | Traces |
|---|---|---|---|
| **What it is** | Numbers over time (counters, gauges, histograms) | Timestamped text lines | The path of one request across services, as a tree of timed *spans* |
| **Answers** | "Is something wrong? How much? Since when?" | "What exactly happened in this process?" | "Where in the call chain is the time / the error?" |
| **Cost** | Cheapest — aggregated | Most expensive — every line stored | Medium — usually sampled in production |
| **Here, produced by** | OTel SDKs, spanmetrics connector, exporters, cAdvisor, RabbitMQ plugin | Every container's stdout | OTel SDKs / agents in every service |
| **Stored in** | Prometheus | Loki | Jaeger |
| **Typical tool habit** | Dashboards & alerts | Search & filter | Waterfall view |

The power is in **moving between them**: a latency spike on a metric panel →
the exact slow trace → the log lines of that trace. Section 6 shows how this
repo wires those jumps.

