### 5.5 Promtail

**What it is.** The log-shipping agent for Loki: discovers log sources, attaches
labels, tails new lines and pushes them to Loki.

**Why it is here.** The services just print to stdout. Promtail collects those
lines from Docker without any change in the applications.

**Configuration here** (`observability/promtail.yaml`):

| Part | Setting | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `clients` | `http://loki:3100/loki/api/v1/push` | Where to send logs |
| `positions` | `/tmp/positions.yaml` | Remembers how far each log was read (lost on restart → may re-read recent lines) |
| `docker_sd_configs` | Docker socket, refresh 5 s | Discovers containers through the Docker API |
| `filters` | label `com.docker.compose.project=ecommerce-demo-docker` | **Only this project's containers** — other containers on your machine are ignored |
| `relabel_configs` | compose service name → `service`; container name → `container` | The two labels you query in Loki |

The Docker socket is mounted **read-only** (`/var/run/docker.sock:ro`) — Promtail
only needs to list containers and read their logs.

**Important:** the filter uses the Compose project name. If you rename the
project (`name:` at the top of `docker-compose.yml`), update the filter too, or
no logs will arrive.

**Common problems.**
- *Some service has no logs* — its container lacks the Compose label (started
  with plain `docker run`).
- *Duplicate lines after restart* — positions file lives in `/tmp`; mount a
  volume for it in long-lived setups.

**Alternatives.** Grafana **Alloy** (Promtail's successor — Promtail is in
long-term-support/end-of-life mode, so new setups should prefer Alloy; the
Kubernetes version of this repo already uses Alloy), Fluent Bit, Vector,
the OTel Collector `filelog` receiver.

