### 5.6 Grafana

**What it is.** The visualisation layer: dashboards, ad-hoc exploration and
alerting across many data sources at once.

**Why it is here.** One UI for all three signals, with click-through links
between them.

**Real-world use cases.** Operations dashboards, NOC/TV screens, business KPIs,
on-call investigation, alerting to Slack/Teams/PagerDuty.

**Configuration here.**

```yaml
grafana:
  image: grafana/grafana:11.2.2
  environment:
    GF_AUTH_ANONYMOUS_ENABLED: "true"      # no login screen ...
    GF_AUTH_ANONYMOUS_ORG_ROLE: Admin      # ... and everyone is Admin
    GF_AUTH_DISABLE_LOGIN_FORM: "true"
    GF_FEATURE_TOGGLES_ENABLE: traceToMetrics
  volumes:
    - ./observability/grafana/provisioning:/etc/grafana/provisioning:ro
    - ./observability/grafana/dashboards:/var/lib/grafana/dashboards:ro
    - grafana-data:/var/lib/grafana
```

> ⚠️ Anonymous Admin is for a laptop demo only. Never expose this setting on a
> shared network.

**Provisioning = configuration as code.** Nothing is clicked together by hand;
everything loads from files at startup:

*Data sources* (`provisioning/datasources/datasources.yaml`):

| Name / uid | Type | URL | Link configured |
|---|---|---|---|
| Prometheus / `prometheus` (default) | prometheus | `http://prometheus:9090` | **Exemplars → Jaeger** via `trace_id` |
| Jaeger / `jaeger` | jaeger | `http://jaeger:16686` | **Trace → Loki logs**, ±5 min around the span, searching for the trace ID |
| Loki / `loki` | loki | `http://loki:3100` | **Derived field `TraceID`**: regex finds `trace_id` / `TraceId` / `traceId` in a log line and links to Jaeger |

*Dashboards* (`provisioning/dashboards/dashboards.yaml` loads every JSON in
`observability/grafana/dashboards/` into folder **E-commerce Demo**):

**Services — RED overview** (`uid: ecom-red`, variable `$service`)

| Row | Panels |
|---|---|
| Golden signals | Throughput, Error rate, p95 latency, Orders paid/min (stats); Requests/sec by service; Error % by service; p95 latency by service *with exemplars*; Slowest operations (top 15, p95) |
| Business metrics | Payments by result/min, Checkouts by result/min, Notifications by event/min |
| Logs | Warnings & errors from all services (click a trace_id → Jaeger) |

**Infrastructure** (`uid: ecom-infra`)

| Row | Panels |
|---|---|
| Containers (cAdvisor) | CPU cores by container, Memory (working set) by container |
| RabbitMQ | Messages ready by queue, Publish/deliver rate, Connections/consumers |
| Datastores | Postgres transactions/sec and connections, Redis commands/sec and memory, MongoDB operations/sec and connections |
| Pipeline health | Scrape targets up |

**How to use it.** <http://localhost:3000>
- **Dashboards → E-commerce Demo** — the two dashboards above.
- **Explore** — free queries against any data source; split view to put
  metrics and logs side by side.
- To change a dashboard permanently: edit in the UI → *Save* is blocked for
  provisioned dashboards, so use *Export → JSON* and replace the file in
  `observability/grafana/dashboards/`, then commit it.

**Common problems.**
- *Panel says "No data"* — check the Prometheus target first, then the time
  range, then the `$service` variable.
- *Dashboard changes lost* — provisioned from files; see above.
- *Data source error* — the back-end container is down; the URLs use Compose
  service names, so they only work inside the network.

**Alternatives.** Kibana (Elastic), vendor UIs (New Relic, Datadog),
Perses (CNCF, dashboards-as-code).

