## 6. How the signals are linked together

| From | To | How it works here |
|---|---|---|
| **Metric → trace** | Latency panel dot → Jaeger | spanmetrics stores **exemplars** (a sample's trace ID); the collector exports them in OpenMetrics format; Prometheus keeps them (`--enable-feature=exemplar-storage`); Grafana's Prometheus data source maps `trace_id` to Jaeger |
| **Log → trace** | Log line → Jaeger | Services print `trace_id` in every log line; Loki data source **derived field** regex turns it into a link |
| **Trace → logs** | Span → Loki | Jaeger data source `tracesToLogsV2` runs `{service=~".+"} \|= "<traceId>"` around the span's time |
| **Trace → metrics** | Jaeger *Monitor* tab | Jaeger reads the same spanmetrics from Prometheus |
| **Across services** | One trace through HTTP and RabbitMQ | OTel propagates the W3C `traceparent` in HTTP headers and in message headers |

The common key is the **trace ID**. Without it, the three tools are three
separate silos.

