## 9. Troubleshooting cheat sheet

| Symptom | First check | Usual fix |
|---|---|---|
| A dashboard panel shows "No data" | Prometheus → Status → Targets | Start the stopped container / fix the target |
| No traces for one service | `docker compose logs <service>` for OTLP errors | Fix `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`; recreate the container |
| No traces at all | `docker compose logs otel-collector` | Fix collector YAML, restart it |
| Config change has no effect | Was the container restarted? | `docker compose restart <component>` |
| No logs in Loki | `docker compose logs promtail` | Compose project name must match Promtail's filter |
| Jaeger empty after restart | — | Expected: in-memory storage |
| Queue depth growing | RabbitMQ UI → Queues → Consumers = 0? | Restart the consumer service; read its logs |
| A database dependant won't start | `docker compose ps` health column | Wait for healthy; check DB logs |
| Docker uses lots of disk | `docker system df` | `docker builder prune`, `docker image prune`; reduce Prometheus retention |
| Mounted file unreadable inside a container (I/O or permission error) | Is the repo inside a cloud-synced folder (OneDrive, iCloud)? | Keep the repo on a normal local disk path |

Useful commands:

```bash
docker compose ps                          # status + health
docker compose logs -f <component>         # follow logs
docker compose restart <component>         # reload a mounted config
docker compose up -d --scale loadgen=0     # start everything except the load generator
docker compose down                        # stop, keep volumes (data)
docker compose down -v                     # stop AND delete all data
```

