## 10. Taking this to production

This stack is designed for learning on one machine. The main gaps before
running anything similar for real:

| Area | Here | Production |
|---|---|---|
| Credentials | Defaults (`postgres/postgres`, `guest/guest`), Grafana anonymous Admin | Secrets manager, unique passwords, SSO for Grafana |
| Data stores | Single containers | Managed services or replicated clusters, backups |
| Jaeger | In-memory all-in-one | Elasticsearch/OpenSearch/Cassandra storage, or Tempo |
| Loki | Sample config, no volume | Object storage (S3), retention policy, auth |
| Prometheus | 3 days, single node | Long-term storage (Mimir/Thanos/managed), HA pair |
| Sampling | 100 % of traces | Head or tail sampling in the collector |
| Alerting | None | Alertmanager or Grafana alerting, routed to on-call |
| Log shipper | Promtail | Grafana Alloy or OTel Collector `filelog` |
| Privileges | cAdvisor privileged, Docker socket mounted | Review and minimise |

The Kubernetes version of this project (`using-kubernetes/`) already moves
several of these forward — see `using-kubernetes/docs/OBSERVABILITY.md`.
